            <div xml:id="d973">

                <pb facs="0868" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg861"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/366: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-08T17:00:00+08:00">September 8, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 8—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>625. Department’s 212, September 3, 9 p.m. and Shanghai’s 630 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">650</hi>], September 4, 3 p.m. British and French
                    Ambassadors, now in Shanghai, are awaiting instructions from home governments.
                    Both favor China accepting proposal emanating from Japanese Consul at Tientsin
                    but are urging home governments to support more ambitious plan outlined in group
                    memorandum recommending Hong Kong and Shanghai bank as trustee bank of deposit.
                    British Embassy states that Inspector General of Customs is urging Chinese
                    Government to accept such a scheme, and that he is being supported in this by
                        Soong.<anchor n="85" xml:id="d973-f1"/> There is a belief that Nanking
                    authorities will be loath to accept any compromise arrangement but there is no
                    definite information regarding Nanking’s attitude as yet. Does the Department
                    wish to take identic or joint action with British and French in support group
                    bank proposal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d973-f1" n="85" xml:id="d973-f1-content">
                <p>T. V. Soong, chairman of the board of directors, Bank of China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
